msgid "wcpcpy"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: build/C/man3/wcpcpy.3:10
msgid "wcpcpy - copy a wide-character string, returning a pointer to its end"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: build/C/man3/wcpcpy.3:19
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"B<wchar_t *wcpcpy(wchar_t *restrict >I<dest>B<, const wchar_t *restrict "
">I<src>B<);>\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: build/C/man3/wcpcpy.3:27
msgid "B<wcpcpy>():"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: build/C/man3/wcpcpy.3:44
msgid ""
"The B<wcpcpy>()  function is the wide-character equivalent of the "
"B<stpcpy>(3)  function.  It copies the wide-character string pointed to by "
"I<src>, including the terminating null wide character "
"(L\\[aq]\\[rs]0\\[aq]), to the array pointed to by I<dest>."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: build/C/man3/wcpcpy.3:46 build/C/man3/wcpncpy.3:75 build/C/man3/wcscat.3:34
#: build/C/man3/wcscpy.3:34 build/C/man3/wcsncat.3:39 build/C/man3/wcsncpy.3:59
msgid "The strings may not overlap."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: build/C/man3/wcpcpy.3:52 build/C/man3/wcscpy.3:40
msgid ""
"The programmer must ensure that there is room for at least I<wcslen(src)+1> "
"wide characters at I<dest>."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: build/C/man3/wcpcpy.3:57
msgid ""
"B<wcpcpy>()  returns a pointer to the end of the wide-character string "
"I<dest>, that is, a pointer to the terminating null wide character."
msgstr ""

