#, no-wrap
msgid "wcpncpy"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: build/C/man3/wcpncpy.3:11
msgid ""
"wcpncpy - copy a fixed-size string of wide characters, returning a pointer "
"to its end"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: build/C/man3/wcpncpy.3:22
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"B<wchar_t *wcpncpy(>size_t n;\n"
"B<                 wchar_t >I<dest>B<[restrict >I<n>B<],>\n"
"B<                 const wchar_t *restrict >I<src>B<,>\n"
"B<                 size_t >I<n>B<);>\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: build/C/man3/wcpncpy.3:30
msgid "B<wcpncpy>():"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: build/C/man3/wcpncpy.3:73
msgid ""
"The B<wcpncpy>()  function is the wide-character equivalent of the "
"B<stpncpy>(3)  function.  It copies at most I<n> wide characters from the "
"wide-character string pointed to by I<src>, including the terminating null "
"wide (L\\[aq]\\[rs]0\\[aq]), to the array pointed to by I<dest>.  Exactly "
"I<n> wide characters are written at I<dest>.  If the length I<wcslen(src)> "
"is smaller than I<n>, the remaining wide characters in the array pointed to "
"by I<dest> are filled with L\\[aq]\\[rs]0\\[aq] characters.  If the length "
"I<wcslen(src)> is greater than or equal to I<n>, the string pointed to by "
"I<dest> will not be L\\[aq]\\[rs]0\\[aq] terminated."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: build/C/man3/wcpncpy.3:81 build/C/man3/wcsncpy.3:65
#: build/C/man3/wmemcpy.3:45 build/C/man3/wmemmove.3:41
msgid ""
"The programmer must ensure that there is room for at least I<n> wide "
"characters at I<dest>."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: build/C/man3/wcpncpy.3:87
msgid ""
"B<wcpncpy>()  returns a pointer to one past the last non-null wide character "
"written, that is, I<dest\\~+\\~wcsnlen(src,\\~n)>."
msgstr ""

